+# R45 / 0.1.32-test.1 — E2LB startup candidate
+
+## Exact baseline
+
+GitHub `1092679281/Android-`, commit `9bc86ce53237b83c23e588e6fa2c7376cca99381`, Actions run `45596424156`, complete-source artifact `15014496262`. Original ZIP SHA-256 `d7e3ea795ee908bd77e3f920511f3f0f532ba63b182df23a57624ca58fcc321b`. Original uploaded APK SHA-256 `843d82355b271bb288adfcef19a21f0213897be13156307830adc2b459dc272a`. This is the actual R44 full-source artifact, not R26 or a decompiled replacement. Inherited fingerprint/evidence files refer to earlier builds and do not verify R45.
+
+## Evidence and scope
+
+The November 26 redacted report shows three sessions ending about 2.3 seconds after availability 0x4300, with no observed ACK for seq 110, three DETECT markers in each observation window and a new SYN. It does not include the raw wire frames or demonstrate why the receiver restarted. The unverified MFi response is not authentication success. No change to wire shape, DETECT response strategy, authentication or receiver identity is made here. No UI/media changes.
+
+## Changes
+
+- Preserve observed-control state at termination; separately record local stream write return and cumulative peer ACK. Synchronous I/O failure retains the receipt rather than discarding it.
+- Classify observed peer renegotiation separately from generic link end. A generated frame or successful local write is not proof of receiver acceptance.
+- Recheck startup cancellation and E2LB link liveness before deriving/returning the endpoint and immediately before publishing it in the shared BT session. This narrows a check-to-use race; does not make external callback delivery atomic with socket closure. Existing originating-link and observation ownership checks remain in force.
+- Make client completion logs conditional on the current generation; do not promise a retry after a circuit breaker or cancellation. Retry policy itself is unchanged.
+- Add explicit Java deque for standalone compiler compatibility and bump base version to 0.1.32.
+- Add synthetic log-order replay for the three new SYN sequence numbers, and a threaded regression for handoff on an already-retired link. These are not captures or a real receiver emulator.
+
+## Verification and limits
+
+51 targeted Kotlin/JVM test methods passed using kotlinc and a minimal JUnit-compatible assertion/reflection harness; no per-method timeout enforcement by that harness (external process timeout applied). Tests cover the engine, transport, receipt tracking and availability classification; Android-dependent callers were not compiled by this run. `git diff --check` and clean-baseline patch application verified. Full Gradle wrapper invocation failed before compilation: Gradle 8.10.2 not cached and services.gradle.org DNS unavailable; Android SDK not configured in this environment. No Android lint, APK, signing or vehicle verification. No repository modification or push. Successful real-vehicle connection requires a fresh, valid authenticated session and evidence of receiver session start/authorized handoff; this patch does not establish that result.
+
+Suggested CI gate from the patched full source: `bash gradlew spotlessApply spotlessCheck :app:testStandardDebugUnitTest :app:lintStandardDebug :app:assembleStandardDebug :app:assembleRemoteDebug` then `bash gradlew :app:testRemoteDebugUnitTest --tests 'com.mcarplay.app.bridge.*'`. Verify artifact package/version/signing before device installation. Do not assume an independently debug-signed APK can upgrade the old debug install.
